<item>
<title>Yemen and the Red Sea: the situation</title>
<link>https://map.igred.org/crisis/yemen/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">igred-summary-yemen-2026-10-24T22:36:59.642Z</guid>
<pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:36:59 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Houthi forces have launched missile and drone attacks on Saudi Arabia, striking Riyadh, Khamis Mushait, Dammam airport and an air base, while Saudi air defenses have intercepted several missiles and drones over Saudi territory. In Yemen, Houthi strikes on Sanaa and Aden have killed civilians, and Saudi airstrikes in Houthi-controlled areas have also caused civilian deaths, including women and children. The United Nations warns that drinking water supplies are dwindling in the besieged city of Taiz and in another Yemeni city under Houthi siege. The conflict caused 918 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/24/houthis-launch-attacks-on-saudi-arabia-and-yemens-aden?traffic_source=rss&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-yemen-s-houthi-rebels-claim-new-attacks-on-oil-facilities-and-airports-across-saudi-arabia&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Times of Israel&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiW0FVX3lxTE1OWDNRWTNxMkEyVlFfSEZmUVlPVlNncENwMDBNck1XNDRWZzEzVDV0VVdzQUx5UW1wZVpwSnN5ZUxlUERKb20ycjUtNExTX1pOeDZva1BiTVFxZUk?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxOeWJ2bGllV1N5MGZKTC1hWXRQUmV5U0xTNll5Q1hTVG1sczNVNjZwNDVuX2NmS2swOFJfOUx0bkpVSGJKWENCZ3AwS2czZ2pXZ3lUOVZXelBMaXZRaUZkX1loWjRndjQ3dXcydFRLdVc3cFQ3ZkRVS2szTTc5S0xtU01CT1hQS0lFX1IxbUNNQk81dzFCbk5wTzhwcHptX0RPejd3eENNdGRLZEM5QmtMMmlUWU9nZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;NPR&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
